KW_AE_{128,192,256}.txt, KW_AD_{128,192,256}.txt, KWP_AE_{128,192,256}.txt, KWP_AD_{128,192,256}.txt, TKW_AE.txt, TKW_AD.txt
    NIST CAVP, the key wrap validation system (KWVS) files of SP 800-38F: KW and KWP with AES, TKW with TDEA, in
    the forward direction (wrapping with the cipher, unwrapping with its inverse).
    Downloaded from https://csrc.nist.gov/CSRC/media/Projects/Cryptographic-Algorithm-Validation-Program/documents/mac/kwtestvectors.zip
    on 2026-10-26. The *_inv.txt files, which use the inverse cipher to wrap (an option of SP 800-38F §5.2 this
    library does not offer), are not included.
    License: NIST CAVP test vectors, a work of the United States government (public domain in the United States).
    Format: CAVP response files; `PLAINTEXT LENGTH` is in bits; an AD record without `P` is marked `FAIL` and must
    not unwrap.
    Used: every record.

aes_wrap_test.json, aes_kwp_test.json
    Project Wycheproof, testvectors_v1/aes_wrap_test.json and aes_kwp_test.json of https://github.com/C2SP/wycheproof,
    downloaded on 2026-10-26.
    License: Apache License 2.0.
    Used: every test: valid wrappings both ways, and invalid ones (wrong integrity values, lengths and padding)
    that must not unwrap.

rfc3394.txt, rfc5649.txt
    RFC 3394, "Advanced Encryption Standard (AES) Key Wrap Algorithm", and RFC 5649, "Advanced Encryption Standard
    (AES) Key Wrap with Padding Algorithm", https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3394.txt and rfc5649.txt, downloaded
    on 2026-10-26.
    License: IETF Trust Legal Provisions; the examples are data.
    Used: the six examples of RFC 3394 §4 and the two of RFC 5649 §6 (KEK, key data and ciphertext).
